WEBVTT

1
01:14:32.522 --> 01:14:34.522
It's a nice movie, isn't it?

2
01:14:36.522 --> 01:14:38.522
This movie is called Risen.

3
01:14:38.522 --> 01:14:42.522
By the way, I want to recommend that you watch a Christian movie from time to time.

4
01:14:42.522 --> 01:14:45.522
I had promised myself to say that.

5
01:14:45.522 --> 01:14:50.522
In the busyness of our society, you read the Word every day,

6
01:14:50.522 --> 01:14:55.522
but how good it is to regularly watch a Christian movie about the Bible.

7
01:14:55.522 --> 01:14:58.522
These have really shaped my faith as a child.

8
01:14:58.522 --> 01:15:02.522
I was always glued to the screen watching all kinds of B-movies.

9
01:15:02.522 --> 01:15:06.522
Often poorly acted, because the budget is low.

10
01:15:06.522 --> 01:15:10.522
But the films, the information in them, were very profound.

11
01:15:10.522 --> 01:15:13.522
And they have strongly shaped my life and my faith.

12
01:15:13.522 --> 01:15:16.522
People read the Bible, but also often watch a movie.

13
01:15:16.522 --> 01:15:18.522
This movie is called Risen.

14
01:15:18.522 --> 01:15:22.522
And you really have to watch it once. It's about the risen Lord.

15
01:15:22.522 --> 01:15:26.522
It's precisely about that resurrection. So let's have a go.

16
01:15:26.522 --> 01:15:30.522
Okay, I'm going to read it. John chapter 21.

17
01:15:30.522 --> 01:15:36.522
After this, Jesus showed himself again to his disciples.

18
01:15:36.522 --> 01:15:39.522
That was by the Sea of Tiberias.

19
01:15:39.522 --> 01:15:41.522
And this is how it happened.

20
01:15:41.522 --> 01:15:46.522
Simon Peter, Thomas called Didymus, Nathanael from Cana in Galilee,

21
01:15:46.522 --> 01:15:50.522
the two sons of Zebedee and two more of Jesus' disciples were together.

22
01:15:50.522 --> 01:15:54.522
And two more of Jesus' disciples is intentionally included,

23
01:15:54.522 --> 01:16:00.522
because we believe that the two unnamed disciples of Jesus symbolize you and me,

24
01:16:00.522 --> 01:16:02.522
who can do great things in Christ.

25
01:16:02.522 --> 01:16:04.522
That's cool, isn't it?

26
01:16:04.522 --> 01:16:09.522
So once again, the saints in Christ are for example Simon Peter,

27
01:16:09.522 --> 01:16:14.522
for example Thomas, who goes for it, for example John, who writes this.

28
01:16:14.522 --> 01:16:16.522
But you are this too.

29
01:16:16.522 --> 01:16:24.522
And therefore, the world is full of great holy people who have done amazing things for God.

30
01:16:24.522 --> 01:16:28.522
And you belong among these people.

31
01:16:28.522 --> 01:16:33.522
You are as it were one of the disciples being taken along by John,

32
01:16:33.522 --> 01:16:35.522
to learn who the risen Lord is.

33
01:16:35.522 --> 01:16:37.522
Isn't that amazing?

34
01:16:37.522 --> 01:16:39.522
Thank you, John.

35
01:16:39.522 --> 01:16:43.522
Verse 3. Simon Peter said to him, I am going fishing.

36
01:16:43.522 --> 01:16:45.522
And they answered, we will go with you.

37
01:16:45.522 --> 01:16:50.522
They went out in the boat, but all night they caught nothing.

38
01:16:50.522 --> 01:16:55.522
When morning came, Jesus stood on the shore of the water.

39
01:16:55.522 --> 01:16:57.522
But the disciples did not recognize him.

40
01:16:57.522 --> 01:17:03.522
Jesus said to them, children, do you have any fish to eat with your bread?

41
01:17:03.522 --> 01:17:05.522
And they answered him, no.

42
01:17:05.522 --> 01:17:10.522
And then he said to them, throw the fishing net on the right side of the boat into the water.

43
01:17:10.522 --> 01:17:13.522
Then you will catch fish.

44
01:17:13.522 --> 01:17:15.522
And they did what he said.

45
01:17:15.522 --> 01:17:21.522
And now they caught so many fish that they could not haul in the fishing net anymore.

46
01:17:21.522 --> 01:17:28.522
The disciple who was Jesus' best friend said to Peter, it is the Lord Jesus.

47
01:17:28.522 --> 01:17:32.522
When Simon Peter heard that it was the Lord, he quickly put on his outer clothes,

48
01:17:32.522 --> 01:17:36.522
for he had taken them off, and jumped into the water.

49
01:17:36.522 --> 01:17:40.522
But the other disciples came in the boat, for they were not far from shore.

50
01:17:40.522 --> 01:17:43.522
But about 200 cubits, that is about 100 meters.

51
01:17:43.522 --> 01:17:47.522
They dragged the full fishing net behind the boat.

52
01:17:47.522 --> 01:17:53.522
And when they had come ashore, they saw there a fire with fish and bread on it.

53
01:17:53.522 --> 01:17:56.522
So Jesus has everything that is needed.

54
01:17:56.522 --> 01:18:01.522
Jesus said to them, give me some of the fish that you have just caught.

55
01:18:01.522 --> 01:18:05.522
Simon Peter went aboard and pulled the fishing net onto the land.

56
01:18:05.522 --> 01:18:10.522
It was completely full, there were 153 large fish in it.

57
01:18:10.522 --> 01:18:12.522
We will come back to this.

58
01:18:12.522 --> 01:18:18.522
And although there were so many, the fishing net did not tear.

59
01:18:18.522 --> 01:18:22.522
Jesus said to them, come and eat.

60
01:18:22.522 --> 01:18:25.522
None of the disciples dared to ask him, who are you?

61
01:18:25.522 --> 01:18:28.522
For they knew that it was the Lord.

62
01:18:28.522 --> 01:18:30.522
Jesus took the bread and gave it to them.

63
01:18:30.522 --> 01:18:32.522
He did the same with the fish.

64
01:18:32.522 --> 01:18:40.522
This was the third time that Jesus appeared to his disciples after he had risen from the dead.

65
01:18:40.522 --> 01:18:50.522
And when they had finished eating, Jesus said to Simon Peter, Simon, son of Jonah, do you love me more than the others?

66
01:18:50.522 --> 01:18:55.522
Simon said to Jesus, yes Lord, you know that I love you.

67
01:18:55.522 --> 01:18:58.522
He said to Simon, feed my lambs.

68
01:18:59.522 --> 01:19:04.522
And then he said to him a second time, Simon, son of Jonah, do you love me?

69
01:19:04.522 --> 01:19:08.522
And he said to Jesus, yes Lord, you know that I love you.

70
01:19:08.522 --> 01:19:11.522
And Jesus said to him, feed my sheep.

71
01:19:11.522 --> 01:19:18.522
And for the third time he said to Simon, Simon, son of Jonah, do you love me?

72
01:19:18.522 --> 01:19:22.522
Peter was saddened that he asked him for the third time.

73
01:19:22.522 --> 01:19:28.522
And he said to Jesus, Lord, you know everything, you know that I love you.

74
01:19:28.522 --> 01:19:32.522
And Jesus said to him, take care of my sheep.

75
01:19:32.522 --> 01:19:38.522
Listen carefully, I tell you, when you were younger you dressed yourself and went where you wanted.

76
01:19:38.522 --> 01:19:42.522
But when you are old you will stretch out your hands.

77
01:19:42.522 --> 01:19:50.522
And someone else will dress you and take you where you do not want to go.

78
01:19:51.522 --> 01:19:57.522
He said this to indicate the kind of death by which Peter would glorify God later.

79
01:19:57.522 --> 01:20:00.522
Do you read this?

80
01:20:00.522 --> 01:20:02.522
Wake up, Cole.

81
01:20:02.522 --> 01:20:09.522
He said that to let Peter know what kind of death he would glorify God later.

82
01:20:09.522 --> 01:20:13.522
That is Effeny Westers.

83
01:20:13.522 --> 01:20:16.522
Effeny belongs in our church.

84
01:20:16.522 --> 01:20:19.522
Couldn't you have overlooked that, Tim?

85
01:20:19.522 --> 01:20:23.522
Isn't it true that if you come to repentance everything will be alright?

86
01:20:23.522 --> 01:20:27.522
And everything is easy from that point on.

87
01:20:27.522 --> 01:20:30.522
Apparently not.

88
01:20:30.522 --> 01:20:34.522
He said that to let Peter know what kind of death he would glorify God later.

89
01:20:34.522 --> 01:20:38.522
And then he said to Peter, follow me.

90
01:20:38.522 --> 01:20:40.522
Follow me.

91
01:20:40.522 --> 01:20:44.522
Following Jesus means leaving everything behind.

92
01:20:44.522 --> 01:20:47.522
Daring to leave everything behind.

93
01:20:47.522 --> 01:20:49.522
Wanting to leave everything behind.

94
01:20:49.522 --> 01:20:57.522
Being willing to leave everything behind that feels easy and stable for us.

95
01:20:57.522 --> 01:21:05.522
It's not that Jesus wants to deliberately put you in trouble, but he wants all of you.

96
01:21:05.522 --> 01:21:09.522
And what could that mean, all of you?

97
01:21:10.522 --> 01:21:12.522
Okay, for those who are taking notes.

98
01:21:12.522 --> 01:21:15.522
I have four V's that you can write down.

99
01:21:15.522 --> 01:21:17.522
The first is fishing.

100
01:21:17.522 --> 01:21:19.522
Then feeding.

101
01:21:19.522 --> 01:21:21.522
Then forgiveness.

102
01:21:21.522 --> 01:21:23.522
And then to follow.

103
01:21:23.522 --> 01:21:27.522
So this story has a lot of content.

104
01:21:27.522 --> 01:21:35.522
And John was deliberately giving content to this story.

105
01:21:35.522 --> 01:21:40.522
And the content of this story, so to speak, are the four lessons I just mentioned.

106
01:21:40.522 --> 01:21:45.522
Fishing, feeding, forgiveness, and following.

107
01:21:45.522 --> 01:21:49.522
Resurrection means you have to go fishing.

108
01:21:49.522 --> 01:21:55.522
The resurrection of Jesus means you have to go feeding.

109
01:21:55.522 --> 01:21:59.522
The resurrection of Jesus means forgiveness.

110
01:21:59.522 --> 01:22:03.522
The resurrection of Jesus means that you will follow him.

111
01:22:03.522 --> 01:22:06.522
These are the four V's that I want to teach you today.

112
01:22:06.522 --> 01:22:08.522
And it starts with fishing.

113
01:22:08.522 --> 01:22:10.522
Verse 5, Michael, can we go there again?

114
01:22:10.522 --> 01:22:12.522
Verse 5, fishing.

115
01:22:12.522 --> 01:22:16.522
So if you made a note, write down for example

116
01:22:16.522 --> 01:22:19.522
The resurrection of Jesus means fishing.

117
01:22:19.522 --> 01:22:22.522
Seems abstract, but here we go.

118
01:22:22.522 --> 01:22:24.522
Jesus said to them,

119
01:22:24.522 --> 01:22:27.522
Children, do you have any fish to eat with your bread?

120
01:22:27.522 --> 01:22:29.522
And they answered him, no.

121
01:22:29.522 --> 01:22:34.522
Then he said to them, throw the fishing net on the right side of the boat.

122
01:22:34.522 --> 01:22:38.522
Then you will catch fish.

123
01:22:38.522 --> 01:22:40.522
Awesome.

124
01:22:40.522 --> 01:22:42.522
They did what he said.

125
01:22:42.522 --> 01:22:47.522
Now they caught so much fish that they could not haul the net in anymore.

126
01:22:47.522 --> 01:22:49.522
Wow.

127
01:22:49.522 --> 01:22:51.522
And a little further at verse 11, Michael.

128
01:22:51.522 --> 01:22:54.522
If you could go there to verse 11.

129
01:22:54.522 --> 01:22:59.522
And Simon Peter went aboard and pulled the fishing net onto the land.

130
01:22:59.522 --> 01:23:01.522
It was completely full.

131
01:23:01.522 --> 01:23:09.522
There were 153 large fish in the net.

132
01:23:09.522 --> 01:23:13.522
When you come to repentance to Christ,

133
01:23:13.522 --> 01:23:21.522
it is intended that your life comes to new life.

134
01:23:21.522 --> 01:23:23.522
When you come to repentance,

135
01:23:23.522 --> 01:23:29.522
it is intended that your old life is buried.

136
01:23:29.522 --> 01:23:34.522
It is intended that there is a transformation in your life.

137
01:23:34.522 --> 01:23:36.522
That cannot be otherwise.

138
01:23:36.522 --> 01:23:40.522
First you were, says Paul, dead.

139
01:23:40.522 --> 01:23:43.522
And now you come to life.

140
01:23:43.522 --> 01:23:46.522
Dude, that's a lot of difference.

141
01:23:46.522 --> 01:23:49.522
First you were a sinner.

142
01:23:49.522 --> 01:23:53.522
And now you have become a new creation in Christ.

143
01:23:53.522 --> 01:23:58.522
If all goes well, a kind of testimony should come forth from that.

144
01:23:58.522 --> 01:24:06.522
If all goes well, you come to repentance and there should be a difference in your life.

145
01:24:06.522 --> 01:24:09.522
If all goes well, there is a change in behavior.

146
01:24:09.522 --> 01:24:13.522
If all goes well, God has done something for you,

147
01:24:13.522 --> 01:24:16.522
through which you have received new life,

148
01:24:16.522 --> 01:24:20.522
and thus you have become completely different.

149
01:24:20.522 --> 01:24:24.522
Old problems must be washed away in the baptismal water,

150
01:24:24.522 --> 01:24:29.522
so that you rise up in Christ Jesus and become a new creation.

151
01:24:29.522 --> 01:24:32.522
Very often in the water, people also say,

152
01:24:32.522 --> 01:24:38.522
yes, I was once this, but I want to leave everything behind and I want to follow Jesus from now on.

153
01:24:38.522 --> 01:24:40.522
A wonderful baptismal testimony.

154
01:24:40.522 --> 01:24:43.522
So when you come out of the baptismal water,

155
01:24:43.522 --> 01:24:47.522
we must also put this into action.

156
01:24:47.522 --> 01:24:50.522
Right?

157
01:24:50.522 --> 01:24:53.522
What do apple trees produce?

158
01:24:53.522 --> 01:24:55.522
Apples, everyone thinks.

159
01:24:55.522 --> 01:24:58.522
Apple trees produce apple trees.

160
01:24:58.522 --> 01:25:02.522
That is the official purpose of an apple tree.

161
01:25:02.522 --> 01:25:07.522
The apple that comes from it is just a fruit containing a seed,

162
01:25:07.522 --> 01:25:10.522
and the seed must become a new apple tree again.

163
01:25:11.522 --> 01:25:14.522
So an apple tree can produce apples,

164
01:25:14.522 --> 01:25:17.522
that people can eat and enjoy,

165
01:25:17.522 --> 01:25:20.522
but the official purpose of that apple tree,

166
01:25:20.522 --> 01:25:24.522
is that it reproduces itself.

167
01:25:24.522 --> 01:25:25.522
Guess what?

168
01:25:25.522 --> 01:25:29.522
The same creator of that apple tree,

169
01:25:29.522 --> 01:25:33.522
who intended for that apple tree to bear delicious sweet fruits,

170
01:25:33.522 --> 01:25:38.522
has also intended for you that you not only bear fruit,

171
01:25:38.522 --> 01:25:41.522
in other words, that you feel better,

172
01:25:41.522 --> 01:25:44.522
and you no longer curse, and you no longer participate in gossip,

173
01:25:44.522 --> 01:25:46.522
but you will speak well of people.

174
01:25:46.522 --> 01:25:47.522
You will encourage people.

175
01:25:47.522 --> 01:25:49.522
You will pray for people,

176
01:25:49.522 --> 01:25:52.522
for the effective prayer of a righteous person is powerful.

177
01:25:52.522 --> 01:25:54.522
And you will bless people.

178
01:25:54.522 --> 01:25:57.522
And what Chris just did, you will sow into people.

179
01:25:57.522 --> 01:26:00.522
You will read the Word of God, and the Word of God will bring life in you.

180
01:26:00.522 --> 01:26:03.522
Streams of living water will flow from your innermost being.

181
01:26:03.522 --> 01:26:06.522
You will reign over the neighborhood where you live.

182
01:26:06.522 --> 01:26:09.522
Your family is intact. Your marriage is intact.

183
01:26:09.522 --> 01:26:10.522
Your children are happy.

184
01:26:10.522 --> 01:26:14.522
You ensure that you have a job and are happy in life.

185
01:26:14.522 --> 01:26:18.522
Your life goes from a wreck to brand new life.

186
01:26:18.522 --> 01:26:21.522
If all goes well, new life should emerge.

187
01:26:21.522 --> 01:26:23.522
Hallelujah, in the name of Jesus.

188
01:26:23.522 --> 01:26:28.522
And so, this new life is not only meant for you.

189
01:26:29.522 --> 01:26:32.522
I once heard,

190
01:26:32.522 --> 01:26:38.522
that almost 90% of all evangelism,

191
01:26:38.522 --> 01:26:43.522
that 90% of all evangelism you do in your life,

192
01:26:43.522 --> 01:26:47.522
you do only in the first five years of your repentance.

193
01:26:47.522 --> 01:26:50.522
Christian psychologists, or whoever studies this,

194
01:26:50.522 --> 01:26:53.522
will make a study of it.

195
01:26:53.522 --> 01:26:56.522
I repeat what Chris just did.

196
01:26:57.522 --> 01:26:59.522
I repeat what I am saying now.

197
01:26:59.522 --> 01:27:03.522
90% of the evangelism you do in your life,

198
01:27:03.522 --> 01:27:08.522
you often do only in the first five years of your repentance.

199
01:27:08.522 --> 01:27:10.522
Why?

200
01:27:10.522 --> 01:27:12.522
Why is this?

201
01:27:12.522 --> 01:27:21.522
Why do we become comfortable in our lives, in our churches,

202
01:27:21.522 --> 01:27:26.522
and the power of fishing decreases, I might say.

203
01:27:26.522 --> 01:27:29.522
Why is this decreasing in our lives?

204
01:27:29.522 --> 01:27:33.522
Why do we not fill ourselves with that worship,

205
01:27:33.522 --> 01:27:35.522
that Vanessa is aiming for in this church?

206
01:27:35.522 --> 01:27:38.522
Why do we not supplement ourselves with worship,

207
01:27:38.522 --> 01:27:40.522
and keep coming to him,

208
01:27:40.522 --> 01:27:42.522
and keep coming to him,

209
01:27:42.522 --> 01:27:45.522
so that he can renew us every day again.

210
01:27:45.522 --> 01:27:50.522
Because, you see, the disciples are here in a boat,

211
01:27:50.522 --> 01:27:52.522
and they say we are going fishing.

212
01:27:52.522 --> 01:27:54.522
And then Jesus comes along,

213
01:27:54.522 --> 01:27:57.522
and they do not recognize him for who he truly is.

214
01:27:57.522 --> 01:28:00.522
He walks along the shore,

215
01:28:00.522 --> 01:28:02.522
and they say, they do not know who he is,

216
01:28:02.522 --> 01:28:04.522
but he gives a command,

217
01:28:04.522 --> 01:28:10.522
because the risen one here wants you and me to become fishers of men.

218
01:28:10.522 --> 01:28:14.522
Something that a faith, which has begun for you,

219
01:28:14.522 --> 01:28:19.522
is now meant for you to live for other people.

220
01:28:20.522 --> 01:28:24.522
Guys, this is next level.

221
01:28:24.522 --> 01:28:27.522
This is not easy.

222
01:28:27.522 --> 01:28:32.522
Resurrection seems to indicate that Jesus has risen for us,

223
01:28:32.522 --> 01:28:35.522
and from the moment He rose for us, everything is ready.

224
01:28:35.522 --> 01:28:36.522
Now it is good.

225
01:28:36.522 --> 01:28:39.522
The intention is, says Jesus,

226
01:28:39.522 --> 01:28:44.522
that you now need to cast your nets in God's kingdom.

227
01:28:45.522 --> 01:28:48.522
You are now called by Jesus to say,

228
01:28:48.522 --> 01:28:53.522
where you were once not successful in gathering people in the name of Jesus,

229
01:28:53.522 --> 01:28:56.522
cast your nets now on the right side of the boat,

230
01:28:56.522 --> 01:28:59.522
so that you can gather people in Christ.

231
01:28:59.522 --> 01:29:07.522
Think about it, when was the last time you were able to reach someone in your life who does not believe in Jesus?

232
01:29:11.522 --> 01:29:13.522
It was a reflective question.

233
01:29:14.522 --> 01:29:16.522
LAUGHTER

234
01:29:21.522 --> 01:29:24.522
But seriously, I want to pause here for a moment.

235
01:29:24.522 --> 01:29:27.522
I just don't want to rush over information.

236
01:29:27.522 --> 01:29:30.522
I want to ask myself this reflective question.

237
01:29:33.522 --> 01:29:40.522
The people in your office, in your class, gym,

238
01:29:40.522 --> 01:29:43.522
market you go to, friends you visit,

239
01:29:44.522 --> 01:29:48.522
are they not placed in your life,

240
01:29:49.522 --> 01:29:55.522
so that you can be the fisher of the people who are placed in your life?

241
01:29:57.522 --> 01:30:04.522
Is the resurrection of Jesus not very simple that His resurrection has become your net,

242
01:30:04.522 --> 01:30:11.522
so that with your life, your business, and your testimony, who you once were,

243
01:30:12.522 --> 01:30:15.522
you can be a testimony for the people around you?

244
01:30:18.522 --> 01:30:21.522
Is it not the intention, for it is not fair,

245
01:30:21.522 --> 01:30:29.522
that you would think that you come to repentance, that we believe in the risen Lord,

246
01:30:30.522 --> 01:30:36.522
but my neighbor who lives right next to me should bring someone else to repentance.

247
01:30:36.522 --> 01:30:39.522
People, we are talking about salvation.

248
01:30:39.522 --> 01:30:42.522
We are talking about the salvation of humanity.

249
